{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792498693,"nonce":"YeF1vVRM5Ff/uNhNZq21kP35TvI=","message":"Implemented viewport-sized Markdown mounts, SCM refresh deduplication, and bounded bridge processing.\n\nMarkdownBlocks uses the existing Ashui Div, Scroll, Owner, Watch and settled-layout APIs. It mounts only the viewport and overscan range in small timer batches. Measured block heights and plain text geometry keys survive presentation disposal; unchanged blocks reuse measurements after edits. The cache contains data rather than editor, image, SVG, canvas or owner instances. Offscreen block owners are disposed, including their CodeViews, bitmaps, diagram controllers and vector registrations. Heading metadata is indexed independently of mounted nodes. Tests cover distant anchors, shortened live documents, disclosure state, scroll restoration and repeated image remount/cleanup in both themes.\n\nSCM no longer refreshes on active.changed. Explicit refresh, saves, remote operations and showing the sidebar remain supported. A visible-only 2.5-second check discovers external changes without replacing unchanged status, refs, history, graph scenes or selected-commit files. A cached workspace root avoids UI round trips during quiet polls. HEAD/ref/focus changes determine when history is walked again. Explicit refreshes that arrive during an existing read are coalesced, and repeated quiet errors are suppressed.\n\nExtensionHost decodes queued messages in short bursts; Connection applies messages with a turn budget and preserves order through shutdown. Studio flushes adjacent operation batches together; Preview updates changed parents/controls instead of rebuilding child placements and flushing every control on every message. Focus requests flush pending views first. Interactions now preempt the existing slow idle poll timer, and disposal cancels that timer.\n\nMeasured with the same Ashui 61510d3 pin and existing shared native targets. AOT large document (7,838 bytes, eight Mermaid diagrams, math, 16 code fences): first-ready time 1570 ms before -\u003e median 624 ms after; longest opening UI turn 1136 ms before -\u003e median 54 ms after (three fresh-process runs, range 51-69 ms). Reopening the cached preview: 1120 ms blocking before -\u003e median 48 ms UI turn after, with median ready time 119 ms. Native node count 2792 -\u003e 508. Hybrid large document opening: median ready 795 ms, median longest UI turn 95 ms; cached reopening median ready 170 ms and UI turn 77 ms. Baseline large-document numbers were single runs; final numbers are three-run medians. The final readiness predicate additionally waits for the visible virtual range to finish mounting.\n\nArtifacts: bin/extension-fixed-{hybrid,aot,stress-hybrid,stress-aot,readme-hybrid,readme-aot}/{summary,results}.json and raw UI/worker logs; rendered dark/light previews in bin/extension-fixed-snapshots/. Initial GPU draw times remain variable, including occasional 0.4-0.8-second first-draw outliers in Git views; these are tracked separately rather than attributed to the VM or claimed fixed.\n\nValidation: core/compiler/embedded-runtime checks; Git native backend suite; full Git and production Markdown UI snapshot scenarios in both themes. A Git test was corrected to wait for its exact commit count and enabled controls rather than matching a number already present in commit subjects. Native app bin/rayde, bin/rayde.hl and bin/RayDE.app rebuilt. No extra Cargo target directories or worktrees; scripts/deps.sh remains the user's unstaged pin change.","files":null}]}